assistants-title = Breadator in ChatGPT and Claude
assistants-description = Connect Breadator to ChatGPT, Claude or another MCP assistant: dough weights, fermentation times and a knowledge base that cites its sources. No Breadator account or API key.
assistants-lead = Connect Breadator to your assistant to calculate dough weights, estimate fermentation times or ask a baking question and get the sources. No Breadator account or API key is required.
assistants-choose = Setup by assistant
assistants-address = Server address
assistants-address-link = the server address
assistants-address-note = An MCP server (Model Context Protocol): { $tools } tools that only read and calculate, plus the articles and recipes, in English and French. No sign-in, no key.
assistants-chatgpt = ChatGPT: web
assistants-chatgpt-account = You need a ChatGPT Pro account (read-only tools) or a Business, Enterprise or Edu workspace that allows custom MCP servers.
assistants-chatgpt-1 = Click “+”, then “Add custom MCP server”.
assistants-chatgpt-2 = Name the connector Breadator. Under “Connection”, paste into “Server URL”
assistants-chatgpt-3 = Under “Authentication”, choose “No authentication”. Review the warning, check “I understand and want to continue”, then click “Create as a plugin”.
assistants-chatgpt-4 = Review the discovered tools, then open Breadator in your plugins and click “+” to install it.
assistants-chatgpt-5 = On the ChatGPT home page, switch to “Work” if you see that tab. Start a new conversation, type @, select Breadator and ask your question.
assistants-chatgpt-docs = OpenAI documentation
assistants-chatgpt-note = These steps are documented by OpenAI; Breadator has not tested the connection in ChatGPT.
assistants-claude = Claude: web, desktop and mobile apps
assistants-claude-1 = Open Claude's connectors, on the web or in the desktop app:
assistants-claude-1-note = In recent versions the page is called Plugins.
assistants-claude-2 = Click “Add”, then “Add custom connector”.
assistants-claude-3 = Name the connector Breadator. For the MCP server URL, paste
assistants-claude-4 = Click “Continue”. Under “Authentication”, keep “No sign-in” (marked “Detected”), then click “Add”.
assistants-claude-5 = Start a conversation and ask your question. To turn Breadator on or off for a conversation: the “+” button, then “Connectors” (or “Plugins”).
assistants-claude-approve = Claude may ask before it uses a tool. “Always allow” stops the question for Breadator: its tools only read and calculate, they change nothing anywhere.
assistants-claude-account = The connector belongs to your Claude account: added once, it also works in the desktop and mobile apps. The free plan allows one custom connector. On Team and Enterprise plans, an owner adds it for everyone under Organization settings, then Connectors.
